Kept already: %s
MSG_KEPT (//)
Kept: %s
MSG_NO_MEMORY_KEEP (//)
No memory to keep the station
MSG_NO_MEMORY_SEARCH (//)
No memory for the search
MSG_SEARCHING (//)
Searching
MSG_ASKING (//)
Asking %s
MSG_NONE_FOUND (//)
No station found
MSG_ONE_FOUND (//)
One station found
MSG_COUNT_FOUND (//)
%u stations found
;
; Why a search or a station failed. A station's reason may have its
; cause after a colon: an answer's status line, a network error's words.
MSG_NO_NETWORK (//)
No network: bsdsocket.library is not there
MSG_NO_HTTP (//)
http.library is not there
MSG_NO_TLS (//)
tls.library is not there
MSG_NO_MEMORY_CONNECTION (//)
No memory for the connection
MSG_SERVICE_NO_ADDRESS (//)
radio-browser.info has no address
MSG_SERVICE_NO_ANSWER (//)
radio-browser.info did not answer the search
MSG_SERVICE_UNREACHED (//)
radio-browser.info could not be reached
MSG_SERVICE_NONSENSE (//)
radio-browser.info's answer makes no sense
MSG_SEARCH_FAILED (//)
The search failed
MSG_NO_SIGNAL (//)
No signal free for the station
MSG_NO_TIMER (//)
timer.device would not open
MSG_LISTS_ONLY (//)
The station's lists lead only to more lists
MSG_STATION_STOPPED (//)
The station stopped sending
MSG_STATION_ANSWERED (//)
The station answered
MSG_SENDS_AAC (//)
The station sends AAC, which is not played
MSG_STATION_ENDED (//)
The station ended the connection
MSG_SENDS_HLS (//)
The station sends HLS, which is not played
MSG_LIST_EMPTY (//)
The station's list names no station
MSG_LIST_TOO_LONG (//)
The station's list names an address too long
MSG_NOT_AN_ADDRESS (//)
This is not an address to listen to
MSG_HOST_NO_ADDRESS (//)
The station's host has no address
MSG_CLOCK_NOT_SET (//)
The clock is not set, so the station's certificate cannot be checked (TimeSync)
MSG_CERTIFICATE (//)
The station's certificate was not accepted
MSG_SECURE_FAILED (//)
The secure connection failed
MSG_CLOSED (//)
The station closed the connection without answering
MSG_NOT_HTTP (//)
The station does not answer in HTTP
MSG_NONSENSE (//)
The station's answer makes no sense
MSG_CIRCLES (//)
The station sends the request round in circles
MSG_UNREACHED (//)
The station could not be reached
MSG_CONNECTION_FAILED (//)
The connection failed
;
; What the shell is told when the Player cannot start: its name first.
MSG_NOLIBRARY (//)
%s: can't open %s\n
MSG_NOMEMORY (//)
%s: no memory for the window\n
MSG_NOBUFFERS (//)
%s: no memory for the sound\n
MSG_NOWINDOW (//)
%s: no window\n
